Published in 1988 by Takarajimasha (宝島社), a Japanese publisher known for cultural magazines and music-related books, the photobook Let It Rock stands as a powerful visual document of THE MODS at a defining moment in their career. More than a collection of band photographs, the book functions as a manifesto of attitude, identity, and era, capturing the raw spirit of Japanese rock as it emerged from the underground and confronted the mainstream. A Japanese rock/punk band from Hakata (Fukuoka) that began activity in the late 1970s, strongly influenced by British mod culture and punk rock. Their sound blends punk rock, garage rock, and mod-inspired;
They made a major impact with releases in the early 1980s, gaining attention for albums like FIGHT OR FLIGHT and memorable songs that became fan favorites.  They stood out for maintaining a rebellious image while achieving commercial success.
